@DarkLight1337 would you mind reviewing this one too, as you did with the earlier Nemotron-Parse PR? It opts Nemotron-Parse into the existing `mm_device_do_normalize` path.

A `ready` label would also help — `pre-run-check` is blocking CI since I'm under the 4-merged-PR threshold, so the new test hasn't run upstream yet.

Validated out of CI on `vllm/vllm-openai:nightly` (byte-identical `nemotron_parse.py` / `mm_input_norm.py` to this branch's parent): bf16 output bit-identical to the host path, served text unchanged with the feature on and off, TTFT p50 263 → 132 ms on one H100.

